------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(b2d) Source saturation by state and round
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A village cannot plausibly have EVERY drinking-water source at once. If a
state shows near-100% presence of tap AND well AND handpump AND tubewell,
its source list is saturated and its 'tap' variable carries no information.
This is a direct test of whether a round is usable, and it is what the
state tables above turn on.
