QUESTIONS FOR THE PI (proposed changes -- NOT applied)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The outcome definitions in code/02_shrug_water.R are unchanged. The
following changes are PROPOSED for your decision:

Q1. 1991 wholesale-missing states. Should the 1991 outcomes be restricted
    to states where tap is not missing wholesale, with the excluded states
    named in the paper? At present the m0 version silently assigns a zero
    to entire states that never reported. See 05a1_miss91_by_state.csv.

Q2. A coverage flag. Should we add a per-shrid flag marking that its
    STATE is wholesale-missing in 1991, so every 1991 regression can be
    run with and without those states without rebuilding?

Q3. 2001 saturation -- the most consequential one. In the states listed in
    (b2d), pc01_vd_tap is 1 almost everywhere because EVERY source is 1
    almost everywhere. Should 2001 be dropped entirely in those states,
    and should a saturation flag be carried per shrid? See
    05b2e_core4_saturation_by_state.csv. This is a question about whether
    the 2001 outcome is usable at all, not a refinement.

Q4. Across-census comparability. On this evidence no across-census tap
    TREND is defensible: 1991 fails in one set of states and 2001 in a
    different set. Should the timing tests be dropped, or restricted to
    the intersection of states clean in every round they use?

Q5. Availability vs functioning. Should any robustness check use the 2011
    _allyr ('Functioning All round the year') variable, accepting that it
    has no 1991 or 2001 counterpart?

Q6. Is the saturation upstream of SHRUG? We have not checked whether the
    2001 saturation is in the Census source or introduced by SHRUG's
    construction. Worth one query to Development Data Lab before we build
    anything on 2001 -- the answer changes whether it can be repaired.

